      "bibkey": "Grave1928",
      "temp": "C2K(15)",
      "units.temp": "K",
      "comment": "['Observation of first release mid-May while the veliger had spent 2 to 3 weeks (mean=17d) in the gill chamber of the females. ' ...\n  'Then, veliger and umboveliger spent 14-30d (mean=21d) of Pelagic Larval Dispersal (PLD) at in situ temperature. ' ...\n  'Then, it takes between 14-21d (mean=17d) to complete metamorphosis after settling (acquiring rasping ridges into its shell to bore the wood). ' ...\n  'First observation of young metamorphosized juveniles at the beginning of July: 17+17+17=51 days.  ' ...\n  '(May temperature 10 C, June temperature in Woods Hole 15 C, July = 19 C)']"
    },
